What is in this repository, and what is not

- Third-party source text is stored here in exactly one place: docs/dr-record-go1-training.json
  and docs/dr-record-go1-training-v1.json embed, as text, three source files of MuJoCo
  Playground 0.2.0 (Apache License 2.0). Each embedded file still carries its own
  copyright and licence header. The v1 record also holds a copy of one Playground function
  with one line changed (the floor-friction range). No other tracked file carries a
  third-party copyright notice or licence header.
- Everything else below is installed or downloaded when the code runs: Python packages
  (pyproject.toml and uv.lock locally; the pins in the Modal image definitions inside
  train/, sweep/, probe/, render/ and app/ in the cloud), the MuJoCo Menagerie assets (which
  MuJoCo Playground downloads while an image builds), and the Rerun web viewer (fetched
  from npm by scripts/fetch_viewer.sh and checked against web/vendor/rerun/SHA256SUMS).
  The Rerun viewer's files were tracked under web/vendor/rerun/ in early commits and were
  taken out of the tree later ("viewer wasm out of git"); the tree keeps only VERSION and
  SHA256SUMS.
- No pretrained weights are used and none are stored here. The two Go1 policies (v0 and v1)
  were trained by this repository's code on Modal and live on a Modal Volume. No dataset is
  used: every rollout comes from the simulator.
- Transitive dependencies are not listed one by one. uv.lock names those of the local
  environment; each Modal image resolves its own when it builds.

Each entry names the file the terms were read from. Where an upstream file names no
copyright holder, none is given here. Licence names for the packages installed locally
agree with their installed metadata; MuJoCo, Brax, JAX, imageio and MuJoCo Playground are
installed only inside the Modal images, so their entries rest on the upstream file alone.

